moment[0] is 1970-01-01 (ISO 8601 writes midnight UTC as the bare date): 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC
its fields: year 1970, month 1, day 1, hour 0, minute 0, second 0, offset 0 minutes, weekday 4 (a Thursday)

The other way: a moment read back as seconds since the epoch
    1970-01-01T00:00:00Z: 0
    1970-01-01T09:00:00+09:00: 0 (the same instant)
    2000-01-01: 946684800

The epoch written in other zones:
    America/New_York 1969-12-31T19:00:00-05:00
    Europe/London    1970-01-01T01:00:00+01:00
    Asia/Tokyo       1970-01-01T09:00:00+09:00
    +05:30           1970-01-01T05:30:00+05:30
(Britain kept summer time all year from 1968 to 1971)

Around it:
         -1 s: 1969-12-31T23:59:59Z
       -0.5 s: 1969-12-31T23:59:59.500Z
      0.001 s: 1970-01-01T00:00:00.001Z
          1 s: 1970-01-01T00:00:01Z
      86400 s: 1970-01-02
2^31 seconds on, where a signed 32-bit count of seconds runs out: 2038-01-19T03:14:08Z
The moments a moment holds lie 100,000,000 days either side of the epoch:
    from -271821-04-20 to 275760-09-13
